cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this model, credit its author and keep the licence file with it.
title: Marocchino (free original 3D model)
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: Mohka Noir
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2022-04-02
abstract: >-
  Redistributed under the author's Apache-2.0 licence (readme/Readme-LicenseText-Full(EN).txt). The
  author's summary (readme/Readme-SimpleLicense(EN-JP).txt) allows redistribution, derivative
  versions, re-upload and revenue, on condition that the original source is credited or the licence
  file is included, and prohibits use for slander or in offensive contexts.
  Marocchino.blend, Marocchino.fbx, Marocchino.fbx.meta, MarocchinoLP.fbx and Textures/ are the
  author's files, unchanged.


  MODIFIED FILES (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)): usd/Marocchino.usda is not the author's file. The
  repository maintainers made it from Marocchino.blend on 2026-09-29 with Blender 5.2.1 LTS (build
  9e2066aef7ef, factory settings), a local conversion tool, and changed the model on the way, in
  memory only (Marocchino.blend is unchanged). The changes: (1) The materials in the .blend link no
  image, so each of nine materials gets an Image Texture node on the Principled BSDF Base Color, the
  link the author's Mire model uses, with the images the .blend itself holds (the Cherry colours):
  Maro.Mt.Face <- Maro.Tx.Face.1.Freckles.png, Maro.Mt.Eyes <- Maro.Tx.Eyes.Cherry.png, Maro.Mt.Body
  <- Maro.Tx.Body.1.png, Maro.Tx.Bikini <- Maro.Tx.Bikini.1.Cow.png, Mar.Mt.CowAcc <-
  Maro.Tx.Acc.Cow.Cherry.png, Maro.Mt.Hair <- Maro.Tx.Hair.Cherry.png, Maro.Mt.Stockings <-
  Maro.Tx.Stockings.png, Maro.Tx.Shoes <- Maro.Tx.Shoes.png, Maro.Mt.Sweater <-
  Maro.Tx.Sweater.Cherry.png. Maro.Tx.Hair.Shade keeps its flat colour; Maro.Mt.Atlas is on no face.
  The author's Unity scene has four colour sets and uses Maro.Tx.Body.2 and the Espresso hair on
  some copies; the export takes the .blend's own images and not the scene's. (2) On the mesh Body,
  the shape keys named with the symbols U+2227 and U+25B2 are renamed u2227 and u25B2: both become
  "_" as USD names, and the exporter then writes 102 blend shape names but 101 targets, which makes
  a USD reader drop every blend shape of the face. (3) Only the object Armature and its nine child
  meshes are exported; ArmatureLP and BodyLP (the low-poly version) are not.
  Maro.Ms.Sweater.VRC is hidden for rendering in the .blend and is exported, because the Unity
  package's FBX carries it. At load, Blender 5.2.1 deletes two shape key blocks that no mesh owns
  (KEKey.000, KEKey.009).


  EXPORT OPTIONS (bpy.ops.wm.usd_export, every other option at its default): filepath=Marocchino.usda,
  check_existing=False, selected_objects_only=True, export_animation=False, export_hair=False,
  export_uvmaps=True, rename_uvmaps=True, export_mesh_colors=True, export_normals=True,
  export_materials=True, export_subdivision=BEST_MATCH, export_armatures=True,
  only_deform_bones=False, export_shapekeys=True, use_instancing=False, evaluation_mode=VIEWPORT,
  generate_preview_surface=True, generate_materialx_network=False, convert_orientation=False,
  export_textures_mode=NEW, overwrite_textures=True, relative_paths=True, xform_op_mode=TRS,
  root_prim_path=/Marocchino, export_custom_properties=True, author_blender_name=True,
  convert_world_material=False, allow_unicode=True, export_meshes=True, export_lights=False,
  export_cameras=False, export_curves=False, export_points=False, export_volumes=False,
  triangulate_meshes=False, usdz_downscale_size=KEEP, merge_parent_xform=False,
  convert_scene_units=METERS. The stage is Z up, 1 metre per unit, rest pose, no animation.
  usd/textures/ holds the nine images the export copied, byte for byte the same as Textures/.
  Two exports of the same .blend write the same prims and values in a different prim order.
